{"name":"Court Jester","hex":"#926d9d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"court jester","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person in colorful garb and fool's cap who amused a medieval and early modern royal or noble court."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/court_jester"}],"entries":[{"title":"Jester","blocks":[{"text":"A jester, also known as joker, court jester, or fool, was a member of the household of a nobleman or a monarch kept to entertain guests at the royal court. Jesters were also travelling performers who entertained common folk at fairs and town markets, and the discipline continues into the modern day, where jesters perform at historical-themed events. Jester-like figures were common throughout the world, including ancient Rome, China, Persia, the Aztec Empire and Medieval Europe."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Heinrich_Vogtherr_d._J._Schalksnarr.JPG/330px-Heinrich_Vogtherr_d._J._Schalksnarr.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jester","wikidata":"Q215548"},{"title":"Court","blocks":[{"text":"A court is an institution, often a government entity, with the authority to adjudicate legal disputes between parties and administer justice in civil, criminal, and administrative matters in accordance with the rule of law."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Microcosm_of_London_Plate_058_-_Old_Bailey_edited.jpg/330px-Microcosm_of_London_Plate_058_-_Old_Bailey_edited.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Court","wikidata":"Q41487"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Fool_or_jester_playing_a_dog_shaped_bagpipe%2C_image_by_Petrus_Gilberti%2C_from_Bible_Historiale_%28Royal_15_D11_folio_262%29.jpg/500px-Fool_or_jester_playing_a_dog_shaped_bagpipe%2C_image_by_Petrus